# J-Link Commander script: clear Cortex-M debug-domain residue (FPB/DWT/DEMCR).
#
# WHY: FPB comparators and DEMCR vector-catch bits live in the debug domain and
# SURVIVE system resets and re-flashing. A stale breakpoint (e.g. Ozone's
# "run to main") makes every standalone boot hit an unserviced debug event at
# that address, which escalates to HardFault - looking exactly like an app bug.
#
# Symptom fingerprint: boot reaches main (or the stale breakpoint address),
# CFSR shows BFSR/UFSR bits or 0, HFSR.FORCED=1, application .bss cleared but
# constructors incomplete, stack may contain garbage return addresses.
#
# USAGE: "C:\Program Files\SEGGER\JLink\JLink.exe" -device STM32F103C8 -if SWD
#        -speed 4000 -NoGui 1 -CommandFile tools\clean_debug_residue.jlink
si 1
speed 4000
connect
halt
w4 0xE0002008, 0
w4 0xE000200C, 0
w4 0xE0002010, 0
w4 0xE0002014, 0
w4 0xE0002018, 0
w4 0xE000201C, 0
w4 0xE0002000, 2
w4 0xE0001028, 0
w4 0xE0001038, 0
w4 0xE0001048, 0
w4 0xE0001058, 0
w4 0xE000EDFC, 0
r
go
qc
